  "question": "The force required to move a body up a rough inclined plane is double the force required to prevent the body from sliding down the plane. The coefficient of friction when the angle of inclination of the plane is $60°$ is",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{1}{3}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$$mg(\\sin\\theta + \\mu\\cos\\theta) = 2mg(\\sin\\theta - \\mu\\cos\\theta) \\;\\Rightarrow\\; 3\\mu\\cos\\theta = \\sin\\theta$$\n$$\\mu = \\frac{\\tan 60°}{3} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$$",
